# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DEV vs LIVE database separation
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Vite loads env files by mode, so testing never touches live customer data:
#
#   npm run dev                -> development mode -> .env.development.local (DEV Supabase)
#   npm run build / preview    -> production  mode -> .env.production.local  (LIVE Supabase)
#
# Both modes ALSO load this shared `.env` (EmailJS + WhatsApp — same everywhere).
#
# The two *.local files hold the Supabase URL + anon key per environment and are
# git-ignored. Create them from these two lines:
#   VITE_SUPABASE_URL=...
#   VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=...
# DEV project  = levaro-tracker-dev  (ref bgprvtqsrkrpwlfubrbu)
# LIVE project = levaro-tracker      (ref cergignhfwrkxgamzfwd)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Shared (this file — loaded in every mode). Copy to `.env`.
VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=your_emailjs_service_id
VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=your_emailjs_public_key
VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_FEEDBACK_ID=your_feedback_template_id
VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_SUGGESTION_ID=your_suggestion_template_id
VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_REVIEW_ID=your_review_template_id

# Business WhatsApp number for customer checkout orders.
# Country code + number, digits only (no +, spaces, or dashes). E.g. 918778044508
VITE_WHATSAPP_NUMBER=your_whatsapp_number
